content.text:
The patch violates ADR-0585. That ADR says `install.sh` "consults no GitHub API endpoint". The patch adds a request to `https://api.github.com/repos/relatedb/relate/releases/tags/$tag` on the failure path. That is an anonymous API call, and it is the shared-IP rate-limit exposure the ADR exists to remove.

I didn't run any tests. Reading `scripts/tests/test_install_sh.sh:134`, the drift guard greps `install.sh` for `api\.github\.com|/releases/(tags|assets|latest)`. The patch adds both strings, so that guard would fail. The test at line 615 would probably also fail, but I haven't checked how it counts API requests, so I've marked it unknown.

